</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="mob-ps-0" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 14px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 21px; padding-right: 20px; padding-bottom: 16px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><strong><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: #223341;">Tuesday 6th May</span>&nbsp; |&nbsp; <a style="color: #223341;" href="https://cvent.me/neKdA2?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=q3clientnewsletter"><span style="color: #48b985;"><u>Register</u></span></a></span></strong></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px; color: #223341;">Join our training led by <strong>Jo Brewin, Consultant, Flywire</strong>, aimed at those responsible for AML. The course will introduce fraud and money laundering concepts; consider the legal position as it applies to the sector; summarise the known activity in the sector; provide guidance to help assess and mitigate risk; outline frameworks to identify and analyse suspicious activity; and provide reporting guidance both internally and to the National Crime Agency.&nbsp;</span></p> </td> 
